| Tight credit minimal impact (net leverage only 1.2x); equity flows matter more |\n| Economic cycle sensitivity | **\u22122** | Affluent consumer travel is cyclical with a lag |\n| Commodity sensitivity | **\u22121** | Fuel (bunker) costs; hedge program likely but unverified |\n\n**1-4. Macro Alignment Judgment**\n\nRegime-weighted impact = 25%(Goldilocks, +1.0) + 25%(Reflation, 0.0) + 30%(Stagflation, \u22120.8) + 20%(Recession, \u22121.5) = **\u22120.41 \u2192 MILD HEADWIND**\n\n\u2192 Conviction \u22120.5 step. No change to intrinsic value; affects position sizing/entry timing.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**1.5-1. Similar-Enterprise Base Rates**\n\n| Question | Base Rate | Applied to VIK |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 5-year survival, established quality consumer grower | ~85\u201390% | VIK: 90%+ survival [Estimate] |\n| Sustained 20%+ growth for 5 more years | ~15\u201325% (most fast growers decelerate) | VIK: 40% probability [Estimate] |\n| Cyclical peak \u2192 40%+ price drop within 3 years | ~30\u201340% | VIK: 35% weight on Bear [Estimate] |\n| Industry capacity wave \u2192 yield compression | ~50\u201360% in cruise/ship-heavy industries | 2027\u20132028 risk elevated [Estimate] |\n| M&A/expansion ROIC > WACC | ~25\u201335% (for large M&A) | New-build ships: ~40% [Estimate] |\n\n**1.5-2. Deviation Analysis**\n\nMy base case assumes ~11% revenue CAGR over a decade. This does NOT exceed the 1.5\u00d7 base rate; for a company with 60%+ repeat guests, 2-year booking visibility and 15% capacity growth, 11% CAGR is in line with, or below, base rate. **No unjustified deviation.**\n\n**1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check**\n\n- Success probability (Bull 25% + Base 50% \u00d7 partial) \u2248 50\u201355% \u2014 does not exceed 1.5\u00d7 base rate (15\u201325% for sustained fast growers)? **It does.** Required additional evidence: (1) 96% of 2026 booked [Estimate]; (2) 2027 already 53% booked, +21% YoY [Estimate]; (3) pricing +10\u201312% [Estimate]. Evidence is strong. No re-evaluation required.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**2-1. Business Understanding**\n\nViking Holdings is the world's largest river-cruise operator and a growing ocean-cruise company, selling destination-focused premium cruises primarily to affluent travelers aged 50+. It operates a fleet of ~96 vessels, sells predominantly direct-to-consumer, and holds a 60%+ repeat-guest rate at ~95% occupancy. Its model is structurally cash-generative: customers prepay fares, producing negative working capital that funds vessel construction.\n\n**Understandability: HIGH**\n\n**2-2. Moat Assessment**\n\n| Moat Type | Score (0\u20133) | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Intangible assets (Brand, Patents) | 3 | Viking brand is category-defining in river cruising |\n| Switching costs | 2 | Repeat guests, but travel agents can redirect |\n| Network effects | 1 | Minimal; some from itinerary density |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Direct-to-consumer saves commissions; not structural |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | ~96 vessels; procurement and marketing scale |\n| Regulatory barriers | 1 | Port/river access exists but is not exclusive |\n| Data moat | 1 | Guest preferences data; modest |\n| **Total** | **11 / 21** | **WIDE MOAT** |\n\n**Moat Direction: STABLE-TO-NARROWING**\n- Widening: repeat rate 60%+, pricing +10\u201312%, 96% of 2026 booked [Estimate]\n- Narrowing: 12 ships delivered 2026, 9 in 2027 across the industry; luxury ocean players (RCL's Celebrity, etc.) adding capacity; low European river water levels raise operational risk [Estimate]\n\n**2-3. Lynch Classification \u2014 FAST GROWER**\n\nCheckpoints:\n1. Growth persistence: supported by aging affluent demographics, China outbound (Mandarin itineraries), 15% fleet/capacity growth \u2014 reasonable for 3\u20135 years, but normalizes after 2028 as the fleet plan tapers.\n2. Balance sheet strength: net leverage 1.2x as of Jun-30-2026 [Estimate]; gross debt $5.74B vs EBITDA $1.79B = 3.2x gross [Arithmetic]; adequate.\n3. No inventory risk: cruise inventory is perishable; 2026 96% booked, 2027 53% \u2014 strong.\n\n**2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard** (all [Filed/Arithmetic] unless noted)\n\n| Metric | Value | Source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Revenue CAGR 2022\u20132025 | **26.9%** (3-yr) | [Arithmetic: (6.501/3.176)^(1/3)\u22121] |\n| Revenue growth FY2025 | +21.9% | [Arithmetic] |\n| Operating margin FY2025 | **+23.1%** (OI $1.502B / Rev $6.501B) | [Arithmetic]; pack confirms |\n| Operating margin 4-yr median | +18.7% | Pack Section 7 [Arithmetic] |\n| Net income FY2025 | $1.148B (17.7% margin) | [Filed] |\n| ROE FY2025 | ~102% (NI $1.148B / Equity $1.121B) | [Arithmetic] |\n| OCF FY2025 | $2.560B | [Filed] |\n| FCF (OCF \u2212 est. capex) | ~$1.26B if capex ~$1.3B | [Estimate \u2014 capex NOT in pack] |\n| SBC as % of revenue | 1.4% (FY2025) | [Arithmetic] |\n| Gross debt / EBITDA | $5.741B / $1.787B = **3.2x** | [Arithmetic/Estimate] |\n| Net debt / EBITDA | ($5.741 \u2212 $3.804) / $1.787 = **1.1x** | [Arithmetic/Estimate] |\n| Interest coverage | OI $1.502B / interest $0.363B = **4.1x** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net cash position | Cash $3.804B; gross debt $5.741B \u2192 net debt $1.94B | [Arithmetic] |\n\n**Judgment: GOOD** \u2014 exceptional growth and margins, healthy liquidity, but gross leverage 3.2x on a cyclical-demand asset base, no dividend, no buyback, and FCF after growth capex is thin.\n\n**2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard**\n\n| Criterion | Score | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Buyback efficiency | 0 | No buyback; SBC dilution (net issuance, share count up from 222M to 440M+ [split-adjusted]) |\n| M&A track record | 1 | Recent acquisition of Viking Yidun (China vessel) \u2014 ROIC unproven [Estimate] |\n| Capex efficiency | 3 | New ships earn strong returns; customer deposits fund much of the build |\n| Rationality of mix | 3 | Clear fleet plan ~$1.5B/2026, $0.92B/2027; self-funding via prepayments |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 | Q2 2026 beat (EPS $1.31 vs guided $1.23); revenue beats consistently |\n| Insider bonus | 0 | Founder effectively controls; no recent insider cluster buying recorded; no large sells identified [Unconfirmed] |\n| **Total** | **10 / 15 + 0 = 10** | **ADEQUATE** |\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2