g (92% booked, 60% repeat) | Behavioral risk: consensus is crowded; one bad Q1 2027 or macro headline hits a 30\u00d7 forward multiple hard |\n| **Crowding Risk Score** | **8/15** | Moderate-high: high inst. ownership + bullish targets + low short | \n\n**Sizing adjustment: \u22121%p for crowding.** Net: Quality-alone capacity 6\u20138%, but price/valuation overrides to **0%**.\n\n---\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nIf presented as a holding within a diversified portfolio:\n\n- **Sector clash**: Consumer Cyclical/Discretionary. Portfolio with existing RCL/CCL/LVS/luxury exposure should cap VIK at <5% combined.\n- **Factor sensitivities**: Dollar (negative), rates (negative-to-neutral), credit (positive float), consumer health (high positive).\n- **Recommendation**: If held, **TRIM OR SELL**. The cyclical nature (beta 1.5) plus negative MoS => risk-adjusted returns are poor. If not held \u2014 DO NOT INITIATE at $92.79.\n\n---\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING\n\n- Edge = (EV \u2212 Price)/Price = (76.50 \u2212 92.79)/92.79 = **\u221217.6%**\n- Kelly fraction = edge / odds \u2248 \u221217.6% / (92.79/76.50 \u2248 1.21) \u2248 **\u221214.5%**\n- **Kelly: NEGATIVE \u2192 0% position.**\n- Note that even at $65 (a 18% discount to my base case), Kelly would only be +2.5%; at $55 it rises to +7%. My buy zone for VIK: **$55\u2013$65** with 50% position at the mean.\n\n---\n\n\u25a0 SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigant |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Recession 2027 (base rate 30\u201340%) | 30% | EPS \u221250%+ (2008 playbook) | Booked float 86% FY26; 38% FY27; 1.1x net leverage |\n| River/European capacity glut | 30% | Yield \u22125\u20138% | Viking brand, #1 share, DTC distribution |\n| Health/geo-political event (new COVID, terrorism) | 15% | Occupancy \u221220pts, revenue \u221240%; liquidity still OK | $3.8B cash + $1.0B revolver |\n| Fuel/crew cost spike (stagflation) | 25% | Margin \u2212150\u2013250bps | Pricing power, fuel-effici